{"reference":"Job 12","book":"Job","chapter":12,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The larger debate","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Job 12 belongs to the sustained debate that follows the friends’ initial seven days of silent presence. In this wider discussion, the friends increasingly explain Job’s suffering by assuming wrongdoing, while Job rejects that diagnosis. This context helps explain the sharp irony of Job’s opening reply and cautions against treating the friends’ later speeches as undifferentiated guidance.","verse_refs":["Job 10:1-22","Job 11:1-20","Job 13:1-28","Job 14:1-22","Job 15:1-35","Job 16:1-22","Job 17:1-16","Job 18:1-21","Job 19:1-29","Job 1:1-22","Job 20:1-29","Job 21:1-34","Job 22:1-30","Job 23:1-17","Job 24:1-25","Job 25:1-6","Job 26:1-14","Job 27:1-23","Job 28:1-28","Job 29:1-25","Job 2:1-13","Job 2:11-13","Job 30:1-31","Job 31:1-40","Job 32:1-22","Job 33:1-33","Job 34:1-37","Job 35:1-16","Job 36:1-33","Job 37:1-24","Job 38:1-41","Job 39:1-30","Job 3:1-26","Job 40:1-24","Job 41:1-34","Job 42:1-17","Job 4:1-21","Job 5:1-27","Job 6:1-30","Job 7:1-21","Job 8:1-22","Job 9:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_job_012_679b4d89c27a69817403ae03"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_2","text":"A later reading of Job associates him with endurance and the Lord’s compassionate outcome. Here, however, steadfastness should not be confused with silence: Job continues to speak, protest, and dispute the explanations offered for his suffering. This broader use of the story’s outcome does not require silent endurance of abuse or prevent seeking protection.","verse_refs":["Job 10:1-22","Job 11:1-20","Job 13:1-28","Job 14:1-22","Job 15:1-35","Job 16:1-22","Job 17:1-16","Job 18:1-21","Job 19:1-29","Job 1:1-22","Job 20:1-29","Job 21:1-34","Job 22:1-30","Job 23:1-17","Job 24:1-25","Job 25:1-6","Job 26:1-14","Job 27:1-23","Job 28:1-28","Job 29:1-25","Job 2:1-13","Job 30:1-31","Job 31:1-40","Job 32:1-22","Job 33:1-33","Job 34:1-37","Job 35:1-16","Job 36:1-33","Job 37:1-24","Job 38:1-41","Job 39:1-30","Job 3:1-26","Job 40:1-24","Job 41:1-34","Job 42:1-17","Job 4:1-21","Job 5:1-27","Job 6:1-30","Job 7:1-21","Job 8:1-22","Job 9:1-35"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_job_012_3859f23efabe4a7326f5a615"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}